    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2TjAz7AF8uUQoE1r8NCDGbJ)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- One PR, two commits; the second (Typst) depends on the first (`sp-note-kinds`). Easy to split if you prefer: the branch could not be split here because only this branch name is allowed.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Three kinds of note, told by Org footnote **label** (`sp-note-kinds`, new):\n  - footnote: any other label (unchanged)\n  - see-also note: `[fn:see-1]`, drawn as a Tufte sidenote\n  - endnote: `[fn:end-1]`, collected in a Notes section\n  - prefixes are options: `sp-note-see-also-prefix`, `sp-note-endnote-prefix`\n- Today (before): `sp-see-also` read any footnote with an `id:` link, inline or numbered.\n- `sp-see-also`:\n  - reads `see-N` notes; endnotes never count; old footnotes still count while `sp-see-also-legacy-footnotes` is non-nil (default)\n  - `sp-see-also-note-new` (`C-; n a`): asks for the note, inserts `[fn:see-N]` and the definition in the `Footnotes` section\n  - `sp-see-also-convert-footnotes` (`C-; n M`): migrates inline and numbered see-also footnotes\n  - cache version 5 → 6\n- Endnotes: `sp-note-endnote-new` (`C-; n e`), template `sp-note-insert-endnotes-section` (`C-; n E`).\n- Numbering: `sp-note-renumber` (`C-; n r`) numbers each kind in text order, so `see-2` before `see-1` is swapped; runs after a new note, `org-footnote-normalize` and Org's footnote adjusting.\n- Org and lint:\n  - `org-footnote-normalize` / `org-footnote-sort` no longer touch these notes (a guard hides them from Org during the call)\n  - `sp-org-lint-footnotes` leaves them where they are\n- Typst (`sp-typst`): `#see-also[..]` (marginalia sidenote, or footnote with `sp-typst-see-also-style` = `footnote`), `#endnote[..]` and `#endnotes()`; `docs/typst/template.typ` and new `docs/typst/sidenotes.typ`.\n- `sp-reading-sidenotes` now draws `see-N` notes through the shared parser.\n- LaTeX mapping: not done (not cheap enough; see the sp-typst doc).\n\n## What was and was not run\n\n- Emacs 29.3 batch: `sp-note-kinds`, `sp-see-also`, `sp-reading-sidenotes`, `sp-keys`, `sp-typst` tests pass; `sp-org-lint` tests pass except two async/batch-view tests that also fail on main in this container.\n- Typst: exported with ox-typst and compiled with the `typst` Python package (0.15.2): footnote, endnotes (`[1]`, `[2]`, reset per `#endnotes()`), `footnote` style, doc without notes.\n- **Not run:** the real `marginalia` package (packages.typst.org unreachable). `sidenotes.typ` was compiled against a stand-in package I wrote, so the call shapes are checked but the margin widths and the look are guesses (version 0.3.1 from its package page).\n- Not run: the whole book with notes, a GUI Emacs, Elpaca, the real vault.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- Definitions all go to the first `Footnotes` heading of the file, not per heading as `sp-org-fn` (not loaded) would.\n- If `org-footnote-section` is ever set, the guard refuses `org-footnote-normalize` rather than risk deleting these definitions.\n- A note cited twice is repeated (sidenote twice, endnote listed twice).\n- Flip `sp-see-also-legacy-footnotes` to nil once the vault is converted?\n- ox-typst declares Emacs 30 / Org 9.7; tested here with Org 9.6 plus a shim.\n\n## Manual test checklist\n\n- [ ] In a litnote, `C-; n a`, pick a note: `[fn:see-1]` appears at point and the definition in `* Footnotes` starts with the link\n- [ ] Insert a see-also note earlier in the text than an existing one: they renumber so the first in the text is `see-1`\n- [ ] `C-c f q` (`org-footnote-normalize`) on a buffer with plain, `see-` and `end-` notes: plain ones become numbers, the others keep their kind\n- [ ] `C-; n r` on a buffer with `see-2` before `see-1` swaps them\n- [ ] `C-; n M` on a litnote with inline and numbered see-also footnotes converts them; running it again says 0\n- [ ] `C-; n e` creates an endnote; `C-; n E` inserts the Notes section once\n- [ ] `sp-see-also-show` still lists mentions from `see-N` notes and ignores `end-N`\n- [ ] `sp-reading-mode`: `see-N` notes show in the right margin\n- [ ] `M-x sp-org-lint-footnotes-dryrun` does not move `see-`/`end-` definitions\n- [ ] `M-x sp-typst-export-file` on a note with all three kinds: sidenotes in the margin (check look with the real marginalia), `[1]` endnotes in a Notes section\n- [ ] Same with `sp-typst-see-also-style` set to `footnote`: no package downloaded\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAHsMuLG5iLMWeAjmt)_",
